WEBVTT

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:08.532
Rust?

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:10.270
That's right, Captain.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:13.541
High levels of ferric oxide...
corroded iron particles.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.548
Would you mind telling me

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:18.551
how iron could rust in space
without oxygen?

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:19.847
I wish I could.

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.911
Mr. Paris,

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:24.389
alter our course to follow
that trail of rust.

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:25.584
One-quarter impulse.

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:27.092
Aye, Captain.

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:37.001
Captain, look at this.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.868
I'm picking up traces
of complex hydrocarbons

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:44.275
in the rust... benzene,
ethylene, acetylene...

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.937
That sounds like gasoline.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:47.105
Gasoline?

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:50.014
It's a liquid fuel that was used
centuries ago on Earth.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:51.014
They burned it

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:53.142
to drive internal
combustion engines.

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:54.744
How did it get out here?

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:56.449
I'm detecting a small object.

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:57.581
It appears to be

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:59.216
the source of the rust
and hydrocarbons.

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:01.124
Put it on screen.

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:03.889
Magnify.

00:02:57.109 --> 00:02:58.633
Apparently, it is
a ground vehicle

00:02:58.677 --> 00:03:00.235
from mid-20th-century Earth.

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:04.648
Whew!
It's a 1936 Ford, actually.

00:03:04.683 --> 00:03:06.116
Mr. Paris?

00:03:06.151 --> 00:03:09.518
That was the manufacturing date:
1936.

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:12.149
Ford was the name
of the company that built it.

00:03:12.191 --> 00:03:14.125
Antique vehicles
are a hobby of mine.

00:03:20.899 --> 00:03:23.732
Internal combustion engine,

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:25.430
a reciprocating
piston cylinder design.

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.962
Fuel source was
a refined petroleum.

00:03:28.073 --> 00:03:29.301
Gasoline.

00:03:29.341 --> 00:03:31.673
So, is this an early hover car?

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:34.770
No, you're about a century
too early for that.

00:03:34.813 --> 00:03:38.909
This is about one step ahead
of the horse-drawn carriage.

00:03:38.951 --> 00:03:42.819
Traces of potassium nitrate,
ammonium and methane back here.

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:45.585
I think you'll find
that's manure.

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:49.857
Horse manure,
if I'm not mistaken.

00:03:49.895 --> 00:03:53.262
Judging from the mud
on the wheels

00:03:53.298 --> 00:03:56.563
and the alfalfa seedlings
stuck in the metal frame,

00:03:56.602 --> 00:03:59.127
I'd say this vehicle
belonged to a farmer,

00:03:59.171 --> 00:04:01.799
or, at least, someone
who lived in a rural area.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:04.741
But the question is:
How did it get here?

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:06.938
I doubt there are
many 20th-century farmers

00:04:07.045 --> 00:04:08.672
driving around
the Delta Quadrant.

00:04:08.714 --> 00:04:10.705
There are no signs
of any wormholes

00:04:10.749 --> 00:04:12.808
or temporal anomalies
in this region of space.

00:04:12.851 --> 00:04:15.877
Let's run a metallurgical
analysis of the vehicle.

00:04:17.623 --> 00:04:19.454
There's still oil
in the crankcase,

00:04:19.491 --> 00:04:21.652
water in the radiator.

00:04:21.693 --> 00:04:23.923
I wonder if the battery's
still charged.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:26.557
Now, let's see.

00:04:26.598 --> 00:04:29.590
This is before
voice-command activation,

00:04:29.635 --> 00:04:33.594
so there should be something
in here called a key.

00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:34.970
Key...

00:04:35.073 --> 00:04:36.734
What are you doing?

00:04:36.775 --> 00:04:39.608
Trying to bring this beauty
back to life.

00:04:39.645 --> 00:04:41.636
Now, where are the keys?

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:44.148
Aha! Here they are.

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:46.981
Okay, choke out,

00:04:47.085 --> 00:04:48.985
clutch in,

00:04:49.087 --> 00:04:50.987
give her a little gas,

00:04:51.089 --> 00:04:53.580
turn the key,

00:04:53.625 --> 00:04:55.354
and step on the starter.

00:05:08.974 --> 00:05:10.134
Sorry.

00:05:12.511 --> 00:05:13.842
Next time...

00:05:13.879 --> 00:05:17.610
you might give us
a little warning, Mr. Paris.

00:05:17.649 --> 00:05:19.082
Aye, Captain.

00:05:20.452 --> 00:05:23.819
I suggest we increase
the ventilation in the cargo bay

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:25.380
before we are asphyxiated.

00:05:25.424 --> 00:05:27.187
What's that?

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:31.185
That is an amplitude modulation
receiving device.

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:33.698
AM radio.

00:05:33.732 --> 00:05:36.257
I'm not sure we'll
pick up much out here.

00:05:39.438 --> 00:05:41.838
Whoa. What was that?

00:05:45.644 --> 00:05:46.906
What is that?

00:05:46.945 --> 00:05:49.243
It's too regular
to be random interference.

00:05:49.281 --> 00:05:51.909
I'm running the signal
through the ship's database.

00:05:53.719 --> 00:05:57.951
It's an ancient Earth
distress call known as an SOS.

00:06:01.059 --> 00:06:03.118
I've located the source
of the SOS signal.

00:06:03.161 --> 00:06:04.822
It's coming from a planet
in a star system

00:06:04.863 --> 00:06:07.263
bearing 310 mark 215.

00:06:07.299 --> 00:06:09.358
Mr. Paris, lay in a course.

00:06:09.401 --> 00:06:10.368
Aye, Captain.

00:06:10.402 --> 00:06:12.370
Why didn't we pick up
this signal earlier?

00:06:12.404 --> 00:06:14.838
This isn't one of the standard
frequencies we monitor.

00:06:14.873 --> 00:06:17.865
Messages on this channel only
travel at the speed of light...

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.935
too slow for interstellar
communications.

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:22.276
Course laid in, Captain.

00:06:22.314 --> 00:06:23.679
Warp 6.

00:06:23.715 --> 00:06:24.943
Engage.

00:06:30.756 --> 00:06:32.383
I'll run
a diagnostic check, sir.

00:06:32.424 --> 00:06:33.721
Mm-hmm.

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:38.291
Bring us out of warp.
Full scan, Mr. Kim.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:41.322
The SOS signal is coming
from the third planet.

00:06:41.366 --> 00:06:43.926
It's Class-L...
oxygen-argon atmosphere.

00:06:43.969 --> 00:06:45.732
Any life signs?

00:06:45.771 --> 00:06:47.966
There's a great deal
of trinimbic interference

00:06:48.073 --> 00:06:49.267
in the upper atmosphere.

00:06:49.308 --> 00:06:51.242
I can't get a clear reading
of the surface.

00:06:51.276 --> 00:06:53.608
Can you pinpoint the coordinates
of the distress call?

00:06:53.645 --> 00:06:54.839
Yes, here it is.

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:57.280
It's coming from a continent
in the northern hemisphere.

00:06:57.316 --> 00:06:58.647
We won't be able to transport

00:06:58.684 --> 00:07:00.208
through this kind
of interference.

00:07:00.252 --> 00:07:02.743
I might be able to take
an away team in a shuttlecraft.

00:07:02.788 --> 00:07:04.255
That would not be wise,
Commander,

00:07:04.289 --> 00:07:06.553
as the atmosphere is charged
with trinimbic turbulence.

00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:07.786
A shuttlecraft

00:07:07.826 --> 00:07:10.693
could not safely
navigate the currents.

00:07:10.729 --> 00:07:13.220
We could land the ship.

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:17.698
Are you sure that's necessary?

00:07:17.736 --> 00:07:20.728
Someone on this planet
is sending out a distress call.

00:07:20.772 --> 00:07:23.332
If that someone is as old
as the truck in the cargo bay,

00:07:23.375 --> 00:07:24.569
they're long-dead by now.

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:26.601
This might be
an automated distress call.

00:07:26.645 --> 00:07:28.306
Possibly.

00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:31.612
But something brought that truck
halfway across the galaxy

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:34.278
and that something
might be down on that planet.

00:07:34.319 --> 00:07:35.946
And if it brought
the truck here,

00:07:35.988 --> 00:07:37.717
it might be able
to take us home, too.

00:07:37.756 --> 00:07:40.748
I'd say it's worth a look.

00:07:40.792 --> 00:07:43.920
Mr. Paris, prepare the ship
for landing.

00:07:45.097 --> 00:07:46.962
Captain,
I think I should tell you

00:07:47.065 --> 00:07:50.728
I've never actually landed
a starship before.

00:07:51.837 --> 00:07:54.499
That's all right, Lieutenant,
neither have I.

00:07:54.539 --> 00:07:56.131
Bridge to Engineering.

00:07:56.174 --> 00:07:57.766
We're going to land the ship,
Ms. Torres.

00:07:57.809 --> 00:07:59.208
Take the warp core off-line,

00:07:59.244 --> 00:08:01.144
vent all plasma
from the nacelles,

00:08:01.179 --> 00:08:03.170
and stand by to engage
atmospheric thrusters.

00:08:03.215 --> 00:08:04.182
Aye, Captain.

00:08:04.216 --> 00:08:07.083
This is Lieutenant Tuvok
to all decks.

00:08:07.119 --> 00:08:08.552
We are preparing
to land the ship.

00:08:08.587 --> 00:08:11.147
Go to Blue Alert and report
to Code Blue stations.

00:08:11.189 --> 00:08:13.180
I've plotted a descent course.

00:08:13.225 --> 00:08:15.693
How close do you want to land
to the distress coordinates?

00:08:15.727 --> 00:08:17.388
No closer than two kilometers.

00:08:17.429 --> 00:08:19.021
Okay.

00:08:19.064 --> 00:08:21.498
Atmospheric controls at standby.

00:08:21.533 --> 00:08:23.592
Landing mechanisms on line.

00:08:23.635 --> 00:08:25.535
Inertial dampers at maximum.

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:27.936
All decks report
Condition Blue, Captain.

00:08:31.243 --> 00:08:32.972
Put her down, Mr. Paris.

00:08:44.589 --> 00:08:45.681
Status.

00:08:45.724 --> 00:08:47.851
We're on the glide trajectory.

00:08:47.893 --> 00:08:50.293
Altitude... 100 kilometers.

00:08:50.328 --> 00:08:52.956
Speed... 10,000 kph.

00:08:53.031 --> 00:08:56.467
Encountering some trinimbic
turbulence. Compensating.

00:09:04.676 --> 00:09:07.736
We have an EM discharge
in the lateral relays.

00:09:07.779 --> 00:09:10.805
I'm rerouting the ODN conduit.

00:09:10.849 --> 00:09:12.373
Another EM discharge.

00:09:12.417 --> 00:09:13.907
I think we're all right, though.

00:09:14.019 --> 00:09:16.112
20 kilometers
to the landing site.

00:09:16.154 --> 00:09:17.951
We should be able to see it now.

00:09:20.659 --> 00:09:21.921
Extend landing struts.

00:09:21.993 --> 00:09:23.927
Prepare to release
inertial dampers

00:09:23.995 --> 00:09:26.486
and adjust them to match
the planet's gravity.

00:09:31.536 --> 00:09:33.333
Landing struts down and locked.

00:09:33.371 --> 00:09:35.601
Standing by
environmental controls.

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:37.972
Here we go.

00:09:47.586 --> 00:09:51.579
Disengaging engines,
securing thruster exhaust.

00:09:53.859 --> 00:09:55.793
We're down.

00:09:55.827 --> 00:09:58.591
Not bad... for a beginner.

00:10:07.672 --> 00:10:09.606
Nice day.

00:10:09.641 --> 00:10:11.131
I've locked on
to the distress signal.

00:10:11.176 --> 00:10:14.441
It's 1.5 kilometers
on a bearing of 246.

00:10:14.479 --> 00:10:16.447
Wait a second.
I've got something else.

00:10:16.481 --> 00:10:19.382
There's a high concentration
of trianium particles,

00:10:19.417 --> 00:10:21.977
bearing 225... a little
over a kilometer away.

00:10:22.020 --> 00:10:23.453
Looks like
some kind of power source.

00:10:23.488 --> 00:10:24.853
Two teams.

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:27.757
Chakotay, yours investigates
the power source.

00:10:27.793 --> 00:10:29.988
Tuvok, Kim, you're with me.

00:10:39.704 --> 00:10:41.331
My God.

00:11:01.193 --> 00:11:03.559
The metal
is an aluminum alloy.

00:11:03.595 --> 00:11:06.257
It appears to be
an ancient Earth aircraft.

00:11:06.298 --> 00:11:09.165
The SOS call
is coming from inside.

00:11:24.749 --> 00:11:26.216
I've found the AM transmitter.

00:11:26.251 --> 00:11:27.616
From what I can tell,

00:11:27.652 --> 00:11:29.677
it's sending out
an automated SOS.

00:11:29.721 --> 00:11:30.710
What about the power source?

00:11:30.755 --> 00:11:31.983
Somehow I find it
hard to believe

00:11:32.057 --> 00:11:35.185
the battery on this aircraft
has been running for 400 years.

00:11:35.227 --> 00:11:37.320
I don't recognize
the power signature.

00:11:41.233 --> 00:11:42.928
Hold on, Captain.

00:11:42.968 --> 00:11:47.871
I found what appears to be
an alien fusion-based generator.

00:11:47.906 --> 00:11:50.739
It's hooked up
to the AM transmitter.

00:11:50.775 --> 00:11:52.640
Chakotay to Janeway.

00:11:54.779 --> 00:11:55.837
Go ahead, Commander.

00:11:55.881 --> 00:11:58.679
We've located the source
of the trianium readings.

00:11:58.717 --> 00:12:00.412
It appears to be
some sort of mine shaft.

00:12:00.452 --> 00:12:02.545
I'd like to bring out
another security detachment

00:12:02.587 --> 00:12:03.815
before we go inside.

00:12:03.855 --> 00:12:04.913
Good idea.

00:12:04.956 --> 00:12:06.651
I'll join you.
Janeway out.

00:12:06.691 --> 00:12:09.057
I want the two of you
to analyze the alien generator,

00:12:09.094 --> 00:12:11.790
then see what you can find out
about this SOS call.

00:12:23.508 --> 00:12:25.806
I'm picking up something
directly ahead.

00:12:25.844 --> 00:12:27.869
Some kind of power signature.

00:12:27.913 --> 00:12:29.278
Fusion-based.

00:12:52.337 --> 00:12:56.000
This looks like some kind
of cryostasis chamber.

00:12:56.107 --> 00:12:58.098
How many bodies are there?

00:12:58.143 --> 00:12:59.440
Eight.

00:12:59.477 --> 00:13:02.674
And the equipment
is still functioning.

00:13:15.827 --> 00:13:17.692
He's human.

00:13:19.831 --> 00:13:21.765
And from the clothes,

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:25.600
I'd say he's from the same era
as the vehicle we found.

00:13:25.637 --> 00:13:27.696
His life sign readings
are minimal,

00:13:27.739 --> 00:13:30.640
but... he's alive.

00:13:33.979 --> 00:13:36.709
Captain, according
to these readings,

00:13:36.748 --> 00:13:40.184
there are five other
cryostasis chambers nearby.

00:13:40.218 --> 00:13:42.311
No life signs in any of them.

00:13:42.354 --> 00:13:45.414
This appears to be the only one
with people inside.

00:13:46.458 --> 00:13:48.619
There's another male over here.

00:13:53.598 --> 00:13:55.225
This one's a female.

00:13:56.234 --> 00:14:00.000
She's wearing
some sort of leather jacket.

00:14:01.606 --> 00:14:03.938
And a pair of gold wings.

00:14:03.975 --> 00:14:05.169
Wait.

00:14:05.210 --> 00:14:07.110
There's a name tag here.

00:14:07.145 --> 00:14:09.739
I think it's "A, period...

00:14:09.781 --> 00:14:11.942
"E-a...

00:14:12.017 --> 00:14:17.045
r-h-a-r-t."

00:14:17.088 --> 00:14:18.783
"Earhart."

00:14:20.492 --> 00:14:24.758
A... Earhart.

00:14:27.232 --> 00:14:29.462
Amelia Earhart.

00:14:33.271 --> 00:14:34.898
Who's Amelia Earhart?

00:14:34.939 --> 00:14:38.397
She was one of the first
female pilots in Earth history.

00:14:38.443 --> 00:14:40.570
In the mid-20th century,
she became quite famous

00:14:40.612 --> 00:14:42.671
for flying across
the Atlantic Ocean.

00:14:42.714 --> 00:14:47.481
In 1937, she attempted to fly
around the world.

00:14:47.519 --> 00:14:51.751
According to the records
of the time, on July, 2, 1937,

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:54.088
Earhart and her navigator,
Fred Noonan,

00:14:54.125 --> 00:14:56.593
took off from New Guinea,
and they were headed east

00:14:56.628 --> 00:14:58.926
around the equator.

00:14:58.963 --> 00:15:02.160
But somewhere in the South Seas,
they vanished,

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:03.724
and their disappearance
became one of the most

00:15:03.768 --> 00:15:05.895
celebrated mysteries
of the 20th century.

00:15:05.937 --> 00:15:07.802
Why didn't they think
she'd just crashed?

00:15:07.839 --> 00:15:09.932
That was the most
commonly held theory.

00:15:10.041 --> 00:15:12.305
However, numerous
searches of the area

00:15:12.343 --> 00:15:14.106
failed to produce the wreckage
of an aircraft,

00:15:14.145 --> 00:15:16.306
so people began to speculate.

00:15:16.347 --> 00:15:18.212
Some thought she'd been
shot down and captured

00:15:18.249 --> 00:15:19.614
by the Japanese navy.

00:15:19.651 --> 00:15:21.812
Others thought that she and
Noonan had flown off together

00:15:21.853 --> 00:15:23.946
on some sort
of romantic adventure.

00:15:24.055 --> 00:15:27.616
Of course,
the most ridiculed notion was

00:15:27.659 --> 00:15:29.752
that she had been...

00:15:29.794 --> 00:15:31.785
abducted by aliens.

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:34.458
Well, it certainly looks
like that's what happened.

00:15:34.499 --> 00:15:35.523
From what we can tell,

00:15:35.567 --> 00:15:37.501
all eight of the people
in that stasis chamber

00:15:37.535 --> 00:15:40.197
were taken from Earth
in the 1930s and brought here.

00:15:40.238 --> 00:15:41.705
The question is: Why?

00:15:41.739 --> 00:15:43.707
And where are the aliens
who did this?

00:15:43.741 --> 00:15:46.301
Scans of the region
show no alien life signs.

00:15:46.344 --> 00:15:47.743
Continue the scans.

00:15:47.779 --> 00:15:49.178
They may not be here now,

00:15:49.214 --> 00:15:52.945
but once they detect
our presence, they might return.

00:15:52.984 --> 00:15:55.544
In the meantime, we'll have
to get some answers on our own.

00:15:55.587 --> 00:15:56.918
Have you had any luck
tapping into

00:15:56.955 --> 00:15:58.354
the computer system
in the cryo-chamber?

00:15:58.389 --> 00:15:59.913
Not as of yet.

00:15:59.958 --> 00:16:03.223
We are having difficulty
decoding the operating system.

00:16:03.261 --> 00:16:05.661
There's one way
we could find out what happened.

00:16:05.697 --> 00:16:08.359
We could wake those people up
and ask them.

00:16:08.399 --> 00:16:10.629
I've had
the same thought myself.

00:16:10.668 --> 00:16:12.135
Is that wise?

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:13.296
We don't know how these people

00:16:13.338 --> 00:16:14.703
are going to react
when they wake up

00:16:14.739 --> 00:16:17.469
in an alien world
in the 24th century.

00:16:17.509 --> 00:16:18.737
True, but I'm not willing

00:16:18.776 --> 00:16:22.075
to just leave them in stasis
for another 400 years.

00:16:22.113 --> 00:16:24.411
And if we can find out
how they were brought here,

00:16:24.449 --> 00:16:27.612
we might be able
to use that method to get home.

00:16:27.652 --> 00:16:31.110
We'll just have to be
very careful how we handle this.

00:16:31.156 --> 00:16:32.453
I suggest
that only human crew members

00:16:32.490 --> 00:16:34.117
be present when we revive them.

00:16:34.159 --> 00:16:35.217
Agreed.

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:37.091
Mr. Kim,
I want a complete analysis

00:16:37.128 --> 00:16:38.857
of those cryostasis tubes.

00:16:38.897 --> 00:16:40.387
Find a way
to deactivate them safely.

00:16:40.431 --> 00:16:42.092
Aye, Captain.

00:16:42.133 --> 00:16:45.534
Commander, apprise the Doctor
of our situation.

00:16:45.570 --> 00:16:47.765
Tell him to instruct Kes
in the proper procedure

00:16:47.805 --> 00:16:50.273
for reviving someone
from cryostasis.

00:16:50.308 --> 00:16:53.436
She could be made
to look human easily enough.

00:16:53.478 --> 00:16:54.638
In the meantime,

00:16:54.679 --> 00:16:57.978
I suggest we all brush up
on ancient Earth.

00:16:58.016 --> 00:17:00.177
We're about to meet
a bit of our history.

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:10.086
We're ready, Captain.

00:17:11.829 --> 00:17:14.696
All the cryo-tubes are linked
by a common power source

00:17:14.732 --> 00:17:17.565
so we've decided to revive
everyone simultaneously.

00:17:18.770 --> 00:17:20.397
Proceed.

00:17:24.876 --> 00:17:27.071
The power's off-line.

00:17:27.111 --> 00:17:29.807
Deactivate locking mechanisms.

00:17:50.969 --> 00:17:53.904
Captain, this one's armed
with some kind of weapon.

00:17:53.938 --> 00:17:56.270
Disarm him,
just to be on the safe side.

00:18:53.765 --> 00:18:55.596
I know this must be
very strange for you.

00:18:55.633 --> 00:18:57.191
No... who are you?

00:18:57.235 --> 00:18:58.463
What is going on here?

00:18:58.503 --> 00:18:59.970
I demand you release me
immediately.

00:19:00.038 --> 00:19:01.801
Please, if you'll just
listen for a moment,

00:19:01.839 --> 00:19:02.806
I'll try to explain.

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:05.331
You are all speaking Japanese.

00:19:05.376 --> 00:19:07.139
Sounds to me like you're
speaking English.

00:19:07.178 --> 00:19:08.509
It's because of a device

00:19:08.546 --> 00:19:11.481
we have...
a universal translator.

00:19:11.516 --> 00:19:13.006
It allows us
to talk to each other,

00:19:13.051 --> 00:19:15.076
even though our languages
aren't the same.

00:19:15.119 --> 00:19:16.313
Who are you people?

00:19:16.354 --> 00:19:18.754
Look, just let us go home.
We won't tell anybody.

00:19:18.790 --> 00:19:19.779
The hell we won't!

00:19:19.824 --> 00:19:21.758
I'm going to let the world know

00:19:21.793 --> 00:19:23.055
what you people have done.

00:19:23.094 --> 00:19:25.119
Do you know
who you've kidnapped here?

00:19:25.163 --> 00:19:26.824
Amelia Earhart.

00:19:26.864 --> 00:19:28.195
I'm her navigator.

00:19:28.232 --> 00:19:30.757
This is going
to be headline news.

00:19:30.802 --> 00:19:32.133
You people are in trouble.

00:19:32.170 --> 00:19:35.230
Fred... let her talk.

00:19:36.441 --> 00:19:39.239
What I have to tell you is
going to sound hard to believe,

00:19:39.277 --> 00:19:41.177
even preposterous.

00:19:41.212 --> 00:19:46.149
We think you were abducted
from Earth... in the 1930s,

00:19:46.184 --> 00:19:48.618
and brought millions
of miles through space

00:19:48.653 --> 00:19:51.884
to a planet on the other side
of the galaxy.

00:19:51.923 --> 00:19:54.858
You were put into a...
a kind of deep sleep

00:19:54.892 --> 00:19:56.860
for a very long time.

00:19:56.894 --> 00:19:59.328
It's not the 1930s anymore.

00:19:59.364 --> 00:20:02.094
The year is 2371...

00:20:02.133 --> 00:20:05.398
over 400 years
from the time you were abducted.

00:20:05.436 --> 00:20:07.768
You must think
we are awfully gullible.

00:20:07.805 --> 00:20:10.569
Tell me, what's the last thing
you remember

00:20:10.608 --> 00:20:12.439
before waking up here?

00:20:12.477 --> 00:20:16.140
We were over the Pacific,

00:20:16.180 --> 00:20:18.307
running low on gas.

00:20:18.349 --> 00:20:20.510
We were looking for an atoll
to set down.

00:20:20.551 --> 00:20:21.518
We...

00:20:21.552 --> 00:20:22.917
tried to send out an SOS

00:20:22.954 --> 00:20:25.479
and...

00:20:25.523 --> 00:20:29.926
suddenly there was this...
huge light in back of us,

00:20:29.961 --> 00:20:31.758
and the plane...

00:20:31.796 --> 00:20:35.823
stopped dead...

00:20:35.867 --> 00:20:38.563
and then it started moving
backward toward the light.

00:20:41.639 --> 00:20:44.005
I must've blacked out, I...

00:20:44.075 --> 00:20:46.009
and I w-woke up here, just now.

00:20:46.110 --> 00:20:47.304
That's just the way
it was with me.

00:20:47.345 --> 00:20:48.812
I was in my truck,
heading into town.

00:20:48.846 --> 00:20:50.837
I was just about to get
onto the blacktop

00:20:50.882 --> 00:20:53.715
when this big light
come down from the sky...

00:20:53.751 --> 00:20:55.480
just about blinded me.

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:56.782
Next thing I know,

00:20:56.821 --> 00:20:59.119
the whole truck
was lifted up off the ground.

00:20:59.157 --> 00:21:01.955
I believe what happened

00:21:02.026 --> 00:21:05.257
was that you
were abducted by aliens.

00:21:05.296 --> 00:21:07.696
And if we can find out
how they got you here,

00:21:07.732 --> 00:21:09.859
we might all be able
to get back to Earth.

00:21:09.901 --> 00:21:13.302
I want some real answers now.

00:21:13.337 --> 00:21:15.134
I assure you,
I am telling the truth.

00:21:15.173 --> 00:21:17.073
You... come on down here

00:21:17.108 --> 00:21:19.303
and get those, uh,
funny-looking guns of theirs.

00:21:23.881 --> 00:21:25.280
You...

00:21:25.316 --> 00:21:26.408
get over there with the others.

00:21:29.120 --> 00:21:30.451
What is this?

00:21:30.488 --> 00:21:31.682
It's a medical device.

00:21:31.722 --> 00:21:33.747
I'm just trying to make sure
that everyone is all right.

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:36.957
Now...

00:21:36.994 --> 00:21:38.325
how do we get out of here?

00:21:38.362 --> 00:21:39.761
Chakotay to away team.

00:21:39.797 --> 00:21:41.196
Janeway here.

00:21:41.232 --> 00:21:43.359
Captain, I'm picking up
some energy displacements

00:21:43.401 --> 00:21:44.368
on the surface.

00:21:44.402 --> 00:21:46.495
I think it may be
alien humanoids.

00:21:46.537 --> 00:21:47.629
It looks like they're using

00:21:47.672 --> 00:21:49.606
some kind of deflection system
to trick our sensors.

00:21:49.640 --> 00:21:51.767
I think you'd
better get up here.

00:21:51.809 --> 00:21:52.901
Who's that talking?

00:21:52.944 --> 00:21:55.777
That's Commander Chakotay,
on our ship.

00:21:55.813 --> 00:21:56.905
Commander, huh?

00:21:56.948 --> 00:21:58.279
Okay.

00:21:58.316 --> 00:21:59.647
Now hear this, Commander.

00:21:59.684 --> 00:22:00.810
There's a gun pointed

00:22:00.852 --> 00:22:04.253
at the lady's head right now,
so you call Washington

00:22:04.288 --> 00:22:06.518
and you tell them we're holding
your people prisoner

00:22:06.557 --> 00:22:07.819
and they're not going anywhere

00:22:07.859 --> 00:22:10.760
until I personally talk
to J. Edgar Hoover.

00:22:10.795 --> 00:22:12.353
You've got one hour.

00:22:12.396 --> 00:22:14.296
Captain?!

00:22:14.332 --> 00:22:17.301
It seems we're being
held hostage, Commander.

00:22:17.335 --> 00:22:20.065
I suggest you pay attention
to what the gentleman says.

00:22:20.104 --> 00:22:21.401
I understand.

00:22:21.439 --> 00:22:22.804
Chakotay out.

00:22:22.840 --> 00:22:24.068
All security personnel

00:22:24.108 --> 00:22:25.735
report to the cargo bay
immediately.

00:22:35.553 --> 00:22:37.180
The compass isn't working.

00:22:37.221 --> 00:22:39.121
I know what we've told you
sounds hard to believe,

00:22:39.156 --> 00:22:41.090
but there was a time
when no one believed

00:22:41.125 --> 00:22:43.559
that a woman could fly
across the Atlantic.

00:22:43.594 --> 00:22:47.121
Now people are able to travel
between the stars.

00:22:47.164 --> 00:22:50.429
The galaxy is full
of many different species.

00:22:50.468 --> 00:22:55.428
For instance,
this young woman isn't human.

00:22:57.909 --> 00:22:59.809
She's an Ocampa.

00:23:02.847 --> 00:23:04.371
I've been on expeditions
all over the world,

00:23:04.415 --> 00:23:05.677
and I've seen people

00:23:05.716 --> 00:23:08.549
do all kinds of strange things
to their bodies.

00:23:08.586 --> 00:23:11.111
That doesn't mean that Martians
have invaded Earth.

00:23:11.155 --> 00:23:12.884
Actually,
it was the other way around.

00:23:12.924 --> 00:23:16.291
Mars was colonized
by people from Earth in 2103.

00:23:16.327 --> 00:23:17.954
That's enough!

00:23:17.995 --> 00:23:20.896
All of you just go over there
and sit down and keep quiet!

00:23:40.051 --> 00:23:41.518
The trinimbic interference
has affected

00:23:41.552 --> 00:23:43.679
the transporter's
targeting scanners.

00:23:43.721 --> 00:23:47.316
We can't beam into the chamber,
so we'll have to go on foot.

00:23:47.358 --> 00:23:48.848
We will deploy throughout
the caves,

00:23:48.893 --> 00:23:50.560
sealing off any exit
from the chamber.

00:23:50.693 --> 00:23:52.183
Let's go.

00:23:52.228 --> 00:23:56.164
Now is probably not
the best time for that, Fred.

00:23:56.198 --> 00:23:57.825
Just a little pick-me-up.

00:24:00.503 --> 00:24:03.631
He's had a few nips
from that flask, Captain.

00:24:03.673 --> 00:24:05.265
We could probably rush him,
get the gun.

00:24:05.308 --> 00:24:07.401
Let me try to talk
to Earhart first.

00:24:07.443 --> 00:24:09.172
She seems reasonable.

00:24:09.211 --> 00:24:10.872
Maybe I can get through to her.

00:24:15.051 --> 00:24:16.040
Miss Earhart?

00:24:25.828 --> 00:24:27.523
I want you to know

00:24:27.563 --> 00:24:30.726
you've always been
an inspiration to me.

00:24:30.766 --> 00:24:33.564
Because of you,
generations of women

00:24:33.603 --> 00:24:35.571
have become pilots.

00:24:35.605 --> 00:24:37.072
Generations?

00:24:39.075 --> 00:24:40.372
What's your name?

00:24:40.409 --> 00:24:41.967
Kathryn Janeway.

00:24:42.078 --> 00:24:45.707
I heard the Commander
call you Captain.

00:24:45.748 --> 00:24:47.716
What exactly do you captain?

00:24:47.750 --> 00:24:50.480
The Federation Starship Voyager.

00:24:50.519 --> 00:24:51.816
Starship?

00:24:51.854 --> 00:24:55.255
That supposed to mean
it flies through space?

00:24:55.291 --> 00:24:56.656
That's right.

00:24:56.692 --> 00:24:57.989
That isn't possible.

00:24:58.027 --> 00:24:59.494
Only in books...
H.G. Wells, Jules Verne.

00:24:59.528 --> 00:25:02.292
Maybe if you saw it,
you'd think otherwise.

00:25:02.331 --> 00:25:04.697
Saw it?

00:25:04.734 --> 00:25:05.701
Where is it?

00:25:05.735 --> 00:25:07.032
On the surface.

00:25:07.069 --> 00:25:10.300
We're actually about 100 meters
underground now.

00:25:10.339 --> 00:25:12.637
If you'd come with me
to see Voyager,

00:25:12.675 --> 00:25:15.439
you'd realize that what
we're telling you is true.

00:25:15.478 --> 00:25:16.775
And risk a trap.

00:25:16.812 --> 00:25:18.780
No, you could have hundreds
of reinforcements up there.

00:25:18.814 --> 00:25:22.045
I assure you, we have
no interest in harming you.

00:25:22.084 --> 00:25:24.450
We took you out of stasis
to help you.

00:25:24.487 --> 00:25:27.923
Put yourself in my shoes,
Captain.

00:25:27.957 --> 00:25:31.290
If you were me,
would you believe your story?

00:25:31.327 --> 00:25:32.487
Maybe not.

00:25:32.528 --> 00:25:35.053
Let me tell you
some of what happened

00:25:35.097 --> 00:25:38.294
after you disappeared
over the Pacific.

00:25:38.334 --> 00:25:39.733
No trace of you or your plane

00:25:39.769 --> 00:25:41.669
was ever found, in spite
of a massive search.

00:25:41.704 --> 00:25:43.103
Over the years, there was

00:25:43.139 --> 00:25:45.505
a lot of speculation
about your flight,

00:25:45.541 --> 00:25:48.135
including the rumor that it was
financed by the government,

00:25:48.177 --> 00:25:49.974
and may have been
part of an operation

00:25:50.046 --> 00:25:52.378
to gather information
about the Japanese.

00:25:53.582 --> 00:25:54.913
Where did you hear that?

00:25:54.950 --> 00:25:57.475
It's somewhat common knowledge.

00:25:57.520 --> 00:26:01.422
You see, Japan attacked
Pearl Harbor in 1941,

00:26:01.457 --> 00:26:04.858
drawing the United States
into a massive world war.

00:26:04.894 --> 00:26:09.763
In retrospect, your journey
was seen in a different light...

00:26:09.799 --> 00:26:11.289
perhaps as part
of an intelligence mission

00:26:11.333 --> 00:26:13.164
devised by a government
deeply concerned

00:26:13.202 --> 00:26:14.260
about Japanese war plans.

00:26:14.303 --> 00:26:17.101
No one was supposed
to know about that.

00:26:17.139 --> 00:26:19.369
Maybe not in 1937.

00:26:19.408 --> 00:26:22.900
Now, it's part of history.

00:26:22.945 --> 00:26:26.881
Hey, I got an idea.

00:26:26.916 --> 00:26:28.747
Why don't we stick them
in these things...

00:26:28.784 --> 00:26:31.309
put them to sleep like we were?

00:26:31.353 --> 00:26:33.787
No fuss, no trouble.

00:26:33.823 --> 00:26:36.883
Mr. Noonan,
that will accomplish nothing.

00:26:36.926 --> 00:26:40.191
Please, let us take you
to our ship.

00:26:40.229 --> 00:26:42.720
You'll see that everything
we've told you is true.

00:26:43.499 --> 00:26:45.797
Show me
how to operate this thing.

00:26:45.835 --> 00:26:48.963
Hey, last time I looked,
you were working for me...

00:26:49.071 --> 00:26:50.868
and I think we should listen
to these people.

00:26:50.906 --> 00:26:52.703
They just may be
telling the truth.

00:26:55.578 --> 00:26:57.102
What's the harm in seeing

00:26:57.146 --> 00:26:59.979
if maybe they do have
this starship?

00:27:00.015 --> 00:27:01.414
It beats being cooped up in here

00:27:01.450 --> 00:27:03.042
trying to figure out
what happened.

00:27:04.320 --> 00:27:06.083
How about it?

00:27:06.122 --> 00:27:07.749
Anyone want to come along?

00:27:11.293 --> 00:27:13.591
Hey, I wouldn't mind
taking a look.

00:27:13.629 --> 00:27:15.654
Anyone else?

00:27:15.698 --> 00:27:16.926
You're not leaving me behind.

00:27:17.032 --> 00:27:19.330
Kes and I will stay
with the others, Captain.

00:27:19.368 --> 00:27:21.768
It'll take about ten minutes
to get to the surface.

00:27:21.804 --> 00:27:23.101
Stay close to us.

00:27:23.139 --> 00:27:24.231
Mr. Kim.

00:27:31.981 --> 00:27:33.380
What is it?

00:27:33.415 --> 00:27:35.110
I am reading energy
displacements again...

00:27:35.151 --> 00:27:38.279
possibly alien life signs...
200 meters ahead.

00:27:58.707 --> 00:28:00.572
They may be up there.

00:28:00.609 --> 00:28:01.598
Take cover!

00:28:01.644 --> 00:28:02.611
Get down!

00:28:16.358 --> 00:28:18.053
This way.

00:28:20.529 --> 00:28:22.520
What's all that racket?

00:28:23.132 --> 00:28:24.099
Take cover!

00:28:24.133 --> 00:28:25.361
I told you it was a trick!

00:28:28.437 --> 00:28:29.665
Fred!

00:28:39.615 --> 00:28:41.082
Janeway to Chakotay.

00:28:41.116 --> 00:28:42.276
I'm here, Captain.

00:28:42.318 --> 00:28:43.478
We're pinned down.

00:28:43.519 --> 00:28:45.111
I can see you from here.

00:28:45.154 --> 00:28:46.382
Lay down phaser fire.

00:28:46.422 --> 00:28:48.447
I'm going to circle around
to your left.

00:28:48.490 --> 00:28:49.821
Try to come at them
from the rear.

00:28:49.859 --> 00:28:50.848
Right!

00:29:00.269 --> 00:29:01.861
Chakotay to Voyager.

00:29:01.904 --> 00:29:03.098
Torres here, Commander.

00:29:03.138 --> 00:29:04.833
Can you give us
some help down here?

00:29:04.874 --> 00:29:06.000
I don't think so.

00:29:06.041 --> 00:29:08.271
The targeting scanners
are still useless.

00:29:08.310 --> 00:29:09.902
I can't risk laying down
weapons fire

00:29:09.945 --> 00:29:11.412
if I don't know
where it's going.

00:29:11.447 --> 00:29:13.108
Keeping trying
to get them on line!

00:29:13.148 --> 00:29:14.376
Aye, Commander.

00:29:23.592 --> 00:29:24.923
Hold your fire.

00:29:24.960 --> 00:29:27.224
Drop your weapons.

00:29:27.263 --> 00:29:29.231
Turn around slowly.

00:29:32.001 --> 00:29:33.298
You're not Briori.

00:29:33.335 --> 00:29:36.395
No, I'm human.

00:29:36.438 --> 00:29:37.735
Human?

00:29:46.448 --> 00:29:47.847
We're human.

00:29:50.252 --> 00:29:52.152
You're working for the Briori.

00:29:52.187 --> 00:29:53.245
They have ships like yours.

00:29:53.289 --> 00:29:54.483
I'll answer any questions
you have,

00:29:54.523 --> 00:29:56.115
but first, we must take care
of our wounded.

00:29:56.158 --> 00:29:57.887
Can we agree to end this?

00:29:57.927 --> 00:30:00.020
Yes.

00:30:01.797 --> 00:30:06.063
I'm Kathryn Janeway of the
Federation Starship Voyager.

00:30:06.101 --> 00:30:08.433
John Evansville.

00:30:08.470 --> 00:30:10.734
This is my colleague,
Karyn Berlin.

00:30:17.246 --> 00:30:19.237
Severe trauma
to the thoracic cavity,

00:30:19.281 --> 00:30:22.341
lacerated carotid artery.

00:30:22.384 --> 00:30:23.442
He's not going to make it.

00:30:23.485 --> 00:30:24.975
I wouldn't be so sure of that.

00:30:25.020 --> 00:30:26.510
Vascular regenerator.

00:30:32.895 --> 00:30:34.294
Hmm...

00:30:34.330 --> 00:30:36.924
he's not responding
to the treatment.

00:30:39.134 --> 00:30:41.159
The alcohol level in his blood
is so high, it's inhibiting

00:30:41.203 --> 00:30:44.104
the repair
to his circulatory system.

00:30:44.139 --> 00:30:47.267
Attempting to compensate.

00:30:49.044 --> 00:30:51.911
I told you your drinking'd
kill you one day.

00:30:54.883 --> 00:30:56.510
She's right, Doc.

00:30:56.552 --> 00:30:59.020
Just let me die in peace.

00:31:03.826 --> 00:31:06.420
There's just one thing
I want to say to you first...

00:31:07.997 --> 00:31:10.158
...even though
it's 400 years late.

00:31:12.334 --> 00:31:14.529
Amelia...

00:31:14.570 --> 00:31:16.037
I love you.

00:31:18.140 --> 00:31:20.802
Fred...

00:31:20.843 --> 00:31:23.778
you never said anything.

00:31:23.812 --> 00:31:25.074
You're married...

00:31:25.114 --> 00:31:27.514
or you were.

00:31:27.549 --> 00:31:28.948
I guess he's dead now.

00:31:31.787 --> 00:31:34.483
I just wanted you to know
before...

00:31:34.523 --> 00:31:36.320
before I met my Maker.

00:31:36.358 --> 00:31:37.586
There.

00:31:37.626 --> 00:31:39.423
That should do it.

00:31:39.461 --> 00:31:40.587
Do what?

00:31:40.629 --> 00:31:42.187
You're healed.

00:31:46.068 --> 00:31:47.729
You mean, I'm not going to die?

00:31:47.770 --> 00:31:50.568
Aside from a hangover,
you're going to be fine.

00:31:52.174 --> 00:31:54.335
Oh, Amelia, you, uh...

00:31:56.578 --> 00:31:58.637
...you got to forget
what I just told you.

00:32:00.215 --> 00:32:01.443
Promise me.

00:32:01.483 --> 00:32:05.214
Fred, I already have.

00:32:05.254 --> 00:32:07.745
Oh...

00:32:07.790 --> 00:32:09.553
You've taken the 37's.

00:32:09.591 --> 00:32:10.785
Why?

00:32:10.826 --> 00:32:12.817
I'm afraid I don't understand.

00:32:12.861 --> 00:32:14.761
You went into the shrine.

00:32:14.797 --> 00:32:17.357
You stole the 37's
from the sacred altars

00:32:17.399 --> 00:32:19.765
and you disturbed
the radio signal

00:32:19.802 --> 00:32:22.202
that we have been so careful
to preserve.

00:32:22.237 --> 00:32:25.172
Captain, I think he's talking
about Earhart and the others.

00:32:25.207 --> 00:32:27.675
Tell me more about the 37's.

00:32:27.709 --> 00:32:28.971
Are you one of them?

00:32:29.011 --> 00:32:30.979
I'm one of their descendants.

00:32:31.080 --> 00:32:34.243
The 37's were brought here
over 15 generations ago

00:32:34.283 --> 00:32:36.717
by the Briori.

00:32:36.752 --> 00:32:37.980
Who are the Briori?

00:32:38.087 --> 00:32:39.987
They're an alien race.

00:32:40.089 --> 00:32:44.253
They abducted over 300 people
from Earth in the year 1937.

00:32:44.293 --> 00:32:47.922
Brought them over here,
turned them into slaves.

00:32:47.963 --> 00:32:49.225
But those slaves revolted,

00:32:49.264 --> 00:32:51.755
killed the Briori,
took their weapons

00:32:51.800 --> 00:32:53.461
and their technology

00:32:53.502 --> 00:32:55.163
and survived.

00:32:57.172 --> 00:33:00.335
And now,
there are over 100,000 of us.

00:33:01.577 --> 00:33:04.045
The Briori never came back.

00:33:04.079 --> 00:33:05.706
Now, you answer me.

00:33:05.747 --> 00:33:07.942
Why did you steal
the remaining 37's

00:33:08.050 --> 00:33:09.074
from the shrine?

00:33:09.118 --> 00:33:12.246
We didn't steal them,
we simply revived them.

00:33:12.287 --> 00:33:14.221
Revived them?
They're dead.

00:33:14.256 --> 00:33:19.250
No, they were simply in a state
of what we call "cryostasis."

00:33:19.294 --> 00:33:20.556
That's a form of sleep

00:33:20.596 --> 00:33:23.064
that appears
very much like death.

00:33:25.934 --> 00:33:27.765
Do you mean they're alive?

00:33:27.803 --> 00:33:29.668
Yes.

00:33:30.839 --> 00:33:34.707
My people have come to regard
the 37's as monuments

00:33:34.743 --> 00:33:35.835
to our ancestors.

00:33:35.878 --> 00:33:39.712
Nobody has even entered
their shrine for generations.

00:33:39.748 --> 00:33:42.444
Mr. Evansville, we were hoping

00:33:42.484 --> 00:33:45.783
to find the ship that brought
your ancestors here...

00:33:45.821 --> 00:33:49.279
possibly use it to get back
to Earth a little faster.

00:33:49.324 --> 00:33:51.622
I'm sorry.

00:33:51.660 --> 00:33:54.925
The Briori ship was destroyed
in the slave revolt.

00:33:54.963 --> 00:33:57.898
There's nothing left.

00:34:00.469 --> 00:34:01.766
Captain...

00:34:01.803 --> 00:34:05.295
I'm sorry to hear
about your long journey home.

00:34:05.340 --> 00:34:09.436
But you should know that life
on this planet is good.

00:34:09.478 --> 00:34:11.810
We live
in three beautiful cities

00:34:11.847 --> 00:34:14.049
only 50 miles from here.

00:34:14.182 --> 00:34:16.616
Oh, I'd like to see your cities.

00:34:16.651 --> 00:34:19.415
And I'd like
to show them to you.

00:34:21.923 --> 00:34:23.618
How fast?

00:34:23.658 --> 00:34:25.353
Warp 9.9.

00:34:25.393 --> 00:34:29.887
In your terms, that's about
four billion miles a second.

00:34:34.769 --> 00:34:36.634
Think I could take her out
for a spin?

00:34:36.671 --> 00:34:37.865
Well, uh...

00:34:39.974 --> 00:34:42.238
Mr. Evansville has offered
to take us on a tour

00:34:42.277 --> 00:34:43.301
of the settlements.

00:34:43.344 --> 00:34:46.871
He's extended the invitation
to the entire crew.

00:34:46.915 --> 00:34:49.008
And the 37's, of course.

00:34:51.986 --> 00:34:53.385
You?

00:34:53.421 --> 00:34:54.683
You're a 37?

00:34:57.692 --> 00:35:00.991
I guess you could call me that.

00:35:06.634 --> 00:35:11.094
It would be an honor
to show you our cities.

00:35:14.175 --> 00:35:18.612
Captain's Log, Stardate 48975.1.

00:35:18.646 --> 00:35:21.615
Evansville wasn't exaggerating
when he said they have

00:35:21.649 --> 00:35:23.310
a lot to be proud of here.

00:35:23.351 --> 00:35:25.148
It was an amazing experience,

00:35:25.186 --> 00:35:29.782
but it's left me
a little disturbed.

00:35:31.126 --> 00:35:32.115
Come in.

00:35:34.963 --> 00:35:36.794
Here's the damage report
you asked for.

00:35:36.831 --> 00:35:38.162
Thank you.

00:35:39.868 --> 00:35:41.358
Is something wrong, Captain?

00:35:41.402 --> 00:35:43.199
You've seemed a little

00:35:43.238 --> 00:35:46.696
distracted ever since
we came back from the cities.

00:35:46.741 --> 00:35:48.174
Weren't you impressed?

00:35:48.209 --> 00:35:51.110
A little too impressed.

00:35:51.146 --> 00:35:52.272
What do you mean?

00:35:52.313 --> 00:35:53.644
There's a thriving

00:35:53.681 --> 00:35:57.845
sophisticated culture on
this planet... of human beings.

00:35:57.886 --> 00:36:01.913
In some ways,
walking around those cities

00:36:01.956 --> 00:36:05.392
was... almost like being
back on Earth.

00:36:07.762 --> 00:36:10.424
It was a little eerie.

00:36:10.465 --> 00:36:12.592
It reminded me of home, too.

00:36:12.634 --> 00:36:15.933
Evansville has offered
to let any of our crew stay.

00:36:16.037 --> 00:36:17.868
What will you do about that?

00:36:19.641 --> 00:36:20.869
Maybe this is
one of those decisions

00:36:20.909 --> 00:36:22.877
that the Captain has to make
for the entire ship.

00:36:22.911 --> 00:36:25.812
You may have a problem
if a lot of people want to stay.

00:36:25.847 --> 00:36:27.212
I know that.

00:36:27.248 --> 00:36:28.943
But at the same time,
I can't take a vote

00:36:28.983 --> 00:36:30.951
every time there's
a major decision to be made.

00:36:31.019 --> 00:36:33.817
And yet...

00:36:33.855 --> 00:36:37.552
we're a long way from Starfleet

00:36:37.592 --> 00:36:39.423
and a lot of the rules
and regulations

00:36:39.460 --> 00:36:43.021
I've learned to uphold
seem distant, as well.

00:36:46.134 --> 00:36:49.365
Am I the only one who is
so intent on getting home?

00:36:49.404 --> 00:36:51.372
Is it just me?

00:36:51.406 --> 00:36:53.874
Am I leading the crew
on a forlorn mission,

00:36:53.908 --> 00:36:58.174
with... no real hope of success?

00:36:58.213 --> 00:36:59.805
You're not alone.

00:36:59.847 --> 00:37:02.680
I want to get home, too.

00:37:02.717 --> 00:37:04.275
And there's not a day
that goes by

00:37:04.319 --> 00:37:06.378
when I don't hear someone
mention Earth.

00:37:06.421 --> 00:37:09.584
The people here have built
a new Earth.

00:37:09.624 --> 00:37:11.251
We could stay,

00:37:11.292 --> 00:37:13.260
help them build
a human civilization

00:37:13.294 --> 00:37:16.058
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:37:16.097 --> 00:37:17.462
Isn't that an exciting prospect?

00:37:17.498 --> 00:37:20.433
Shouldn't we be grateful
for the opportunity

00:37:20.468 --> 00:37:21.799
they're giving us?

00:37:21.836 --> 00:37:23.599
It is a tempting prospect.

00:37:25.940 --> 00:37:27.635
But when I hold it up
against the prospect

00:37:27.675 --> 00:37:30.371
of seeing the sunrise
over the Arizona desert

00:37:30.411 --> 00:37:35.348
or swimming in the Gulf
of Mexico on a summer's day,

00:37:35.383 --> 00:37:38.113
there's just no comparison.

00:37:38.152 --> 00:37:39.949
I want to go home.

00:37:40.021 --> 00:37:44.481
We have 152 men and women
on this ship.

00:37:44.525 --> 00:37:48.552
What happens if half of them
decide to stay on the planet?

00:37:48.596 --> 00:37:51.463
Could we operate Voyager
with 75 crew members?

00:37:51.499 --> 00:37:52.466
I doubt it.

00:37:52.500 --> 00:37:53.762
In fact, I don't think

00:37:53.801 --> 00:37:56.269
we could operate the ship
with fewer than 100.

00:37:56.304 --> 00:37:59.432
If too many of the crew
choose to stay behind...

00:37:59.474 --> 00:38:01.704
we could all be stranded here.

00:38:05.246 --> 00:38:07.737
Tell all hands to prepare for
an announcement from the Captain

00:38:07.782 --> 00:38:09.773
at 1400 hours.

00:38:12.020 --> 00:38:14.750
They deserve to make the choice
for themselves.

00:38:14.789 --> 00:38:16.347
Aye, Captain.

00:38:34.509 --> 00:38:35.840
Here we are.

00:38:35.877 --> 00:38:39.608
My research on 20th century
Earth is a little thin,

00:38:39.647 --> 00:38:42.138
but I've done what I can.

00:38:42.183 --> 00:38:44.083
Pot roast, green beans

00:38:44.118 --> 00:38:47.645
and something called...
Jell... O.

00:38:47.689 --> 00:38:49.520
You know how to make Jell-O?

00:38:49.557 --> 00:38:51.354
I even put in fruit cocktail.

00:38:51.392 --> 00:38:53.087
You don't say.

00:38:53.127 --> 00:38:55.095
I don't know
about the rest of you,

00:38:55.129 --> 00:38:56.596
but I've made up my mind.

00:38:56.631 --> 00:39:00.089
There is land here
that goes begging,

00:39:00.134 --> 00:39:03.331
and I could have a big farm,
just like I always dreamed.

00:39:03.371 --> 00:39:07.000
And for you, rice,
with a little fish.

00:39:07.041 --> 00:39:10.442
I even replicated
some ginger for seasoning.

00:39:10.478 --> 00:39:11.911
Very nice.

00:39:11.946 --> 00:39:14.346
Thank you.

00:39:14.382 --> 00:39:16.111
Yeah, I have to admit...

00:39:16.150 --> 00:39:19.142
life here looks a lot better
than what we left on Earth.

00:39:19.187 --> 00:39:21.417
It's a paradise by comparison.

00:39:21.456 --> 00:39:23.890
And there are
many Japanese here.

00:39:23.925 --> 00:39:26.485
I could be very happy.

00:39:26.527 --> 00:39:28.256
We all could.

00:39:28.296 --> 00:39:29.627
Right?

00:39:32.633 --> 00:39:35.295
I'm just not sure, I...

00:39:35.336 --> 00:39:37.827
What about you, Mr. Neelix?

00:39:37.872 --> 00:39:39.931
Have you made your decision?

00:39:39.974 --> 00:39:41.271
Oh, yes, indeed.

00:39:41.309 --> 00:39:43.743
I'm staying right here
with Captain Janeway.

00:39:43.778 --> 00:39:45.370
She'd be lost without me.

00:39:45.413 --> 00:39:49.213
She's come to depend on me
a great deal.

00:39:49.250 --> 00:39:50.410
What about the rest of the crew?

00:39:50.451 --> 00:39:52.419
You think many of them
will stay here?

00:39:52.453 --> 00:39:54.421
Oh, I don't think so.

00:39:54.455 --> 00:39:55.683
At least, not many.

00:39:55.723 --> 00:39:59.955
Uh, well, that is,
there's a good chance...

00:40:00.027 --> 00:40:03.360
Well, now that you ask,
I honestly don't know.

00:40:03.398 --> 00:40:04.524
You?

00:40:04.565 --> 00:40:06.396
You'd stay here on the planet?

00:40:06.434 --> 00:40:08.197
I didn't say I was going to.

00:40:08.236 --> 00:40:12.332
I just said I could understand
why people would want to.

00:40:12.373 --> 00:40:14.705
The people here
remind me of home.

00:40:14.742 --> 00:40:17.836
I haven't felt like that
since I left Earth.

00:40:17.879 --> 00:40:21.337
But... but you're Starfleet.

00:40:21.382 --> 00:40:23.543
You've always wanted
a life in space.

00:40:23.584 --> 00:40:24.551
I know,

00:40:24.585 --> 00:40:26.917
but... my whole life?

00:40:26.954 --> 00:40:30.720
On a starship, day after day,
with no end in sight?

00:40:30.758 --> 00:40:33.488
That's not exactly
what I had in mind.

00:40:33.528 --> 00:40:36.463
You're not the first person
I've heard talk like this.

00:40:36.497 --> 00:40:38.863
A lot of people
are thinking about staying.

00:40:38.900 --> 00:40:41.494
What about you?

00:40:41.536 --> 00:40:43.834
Don't you have
some of those feelings?

00:40:43.871 --> 00:40:47.102
I'd be lying if I said I didn't.

00:40:55.116 --> 00:40:56.845
Captain.

00:40:56.884 --> 00:40:57.908
I was told I'd find you here.

00:40:57.952 --> 00:40:58.919
Am I intruding?

00:40:58.953 --> 00:40:59.920
Not at all.

00:40:59.954 --> 00:41:01.888
Please join me.

00:41:01.923 --> 00:41:04.585
I wanted you to know that

00:41:04.625 --> 00:41:07.423
the group you brought
out of stasis...

00:41:07.462 --> 00:41:09.794
we've all decided to stay here
on the planet.

00:41:13.067 --> 00:41:14.830
I understand.

00:41:14.869 --> 00:41:18.669
I must admit, the thought
of traveling through space...

00:41:18.706 --> 00:41:21.971
maybe even learning
to fly this ship...

00:41:22.043 --> 00:41:24.170
was very appealing to me.

00:41:24.212 --> 00:41:26.976
And I'd looked forward
to getting to know you better.

00:41:27.048 --> 00:41:29.881
I suspect we have
a lot in common.

00:41:32.353 --> 00:41:35.151
At first,
I didn't know what to do.

00:41:35.189 --> 00:41:38.420
We talked about it
for quite some time.

00:41:38.459 --> 00:41:42.657
Finally, I realized
the people here on this planet

00:41:42.697 --> 00:41:44.665
are part of us.

00:41:44.699 --> 00:41:47.167
We're their ancestors, in a way.

00:41:47.201 --> 00:41:51.228
Well, it made us
feel close to them.

00:41:51.272 --> 00:41:53.832
The remarkable thing about
the humans on this planet

00:41:53.875 --> 00:41:57.504
is that they evolved very much
like the people on Earth.

00:41:57.545 --> 00:42:00.343
Tens of thousands
of light-years apart,

00:42:00.381 --> 00:42:03.077
both civilizations
managed to create a world

00:42:03.117 --> 00:42:04.846
they could be proud of...

00:42:04.886 --> 00:42:08.344
one where war and poverty
simply don't exist.

00:42:08.389 --> 00:42:12.758
I certainly can't blame you
for wanting to be part of it,

00:42:12.793 --> 00:42:15.455
any more than I can blame
members of my crew

00:42:15.496 --> 00:42:17.623
if they make the same decision.

00:42:17.665 --> 00:42:19.565
When will you find out?

00:42:19.600 --> 00:42:21.192
In half an hour.

00:42:21.235 --> 00:42:23.203
Anyone who wants to stay behind

00:42:23.237 --> 00:42:26.764
is to report to the
cargo bay at 1500 hours.

00:42:29.110 --> 00:42:31.101
I expect Jarvin will
stay on the planet.

00:42:31.145 --> 00:42:32.305
In fact, I'd bet on it.

00:42:32.346 --> 00:42:33.904
Why Jarvin?

00:42:33.948 --> 00:42:36.280
He's been more uncomfortable
about being on a Starfleet ship

00:42:36.317 --> 00:42:37.807
than most of the Maquis.

00:42:37.852 --> 00:42:38.978
And he's gotten involved

00:42:39.086 --> 00:42:41.077
with a young woman
in Quantum Mechanics.

00:42:41.122 --> 00:42:44.148
I think they'd like to
settle down, raise a family.

00:42:44.191 --> 00:42:46.250
The person I expect
to see is Baxter.

00:42:46.294 --> 00:42:48.125
Baxter?
Walter Baxter?

00:42:48.162 --> 00:42:50.153
He's adventurous, a risk-taker.

00:42:50.197 --> 00:42:51.858
I can see him wanting
to take on the challenge

00:42:51.899 --> 00:42:54.231
of building a new life
on this planet.

00:42:54.268 --> 00:42:56.133
I'd hate to lose Baxter.

00:42:56.170 --> 00:42:57.159
He's a good man.

00:42:57.204 --> 00:42:58.796
I'd hate to lose Jarvin.

00:43:00.207 --> 00:43:02.869
I don't want to lose anyone.

00:43:02.910 --> 00:43:04.673
We've all been through
so much together,

00:43:04.712 --> 00:43:06.009
it just wouldn't seem right.

00:43:07.448 --> 00:43:09.939
But I couldn't blame anyone...

00:43:09.984 --> 00:43:13.545
anyone... for staying behind.

00:43:15.923 --> 00:43:18.915
I'm not sure I want to go in.

00:43:21.729 --> 00:43:25.221
No matter what happens,
we'll make it.

00:43:25.266 --> 00:43:27.257
Remember that.

00:43:51.959 --> 00:43:53.449
Captain on the Bridge.

00:44:17.752 --> 00:44:20.312
All stations,
prepare for departure.

00:44:20.354 --> 00:44:21.821
Condition Blue, Mr. Tuvok.

00:44:21.856 --> 00:44:24.791
Ms. Torres,
antigrav thrusters on line.

00:44:24.825 --> 00:44:26.087
Thrusters enabled.

00:44:26.127 --> 00:44:27.094
Mr. Paris,

00:44:27.128 --> 00:44:28.959
inertial dampers
to flight configuration.

00:44:29.030 --> 00:44:31.396
Impulse drive to standby.

00:44:31.432 --> 00:44:33.161
Yes, ma'am.

00:44:35.336 --> 00:44:37.964
All stations report ready,
Captain.

00:44:38.039 --> 00:44:40.303
Then let's do it.

00:44:40.341 --> 00:44:42.502
Take us up.
